# Not required for local development -- Vite's dev proxy (vite.config.js)
# already forwards /api and /ws to http://localhost:8000, so the app works
# with zero env vars out of the box as long as the backend runs on its
# default port 8000.
#
# Only set this if you're running the backend on a different host/port
# (e.g. deploying the built frontend separately from the backend) and want
# the app to talk to it directly instead of through Vite's dev proxy.
# Copy this file to ".env" and uncomment/edit as needed.

# VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8000
